  "title": "json.c: Limit memory allocation to file size",
  "description": "Currently, json.c allocates `MAX_FILE_SIZE` bytes (50 MB) as part of checking if a file is valid JSON. This limits the memory allocation to the file's size, to lower the number of large memory allocations.",
